{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 is the rider's principal route to a no-fault refund on coordination grounds, and its limb (a) fails outright. Limb (a) requires at least one message from the RIDER during the waiting window whose content is locating or coordinating — their own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that they cannot see the vehicle. The chat log runs from 08:43:00 to 08:51:00 and holds six entries; every one is from the DRIVER or the SYSTEM. The rider never asked where the car was, never named an entrance or bay, and never said they could not find the vehicle. Limb (a) is not met, so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if limb (a) were somehow met, POL-NS-04 limb (b) is affirmatively failed. The clause requires that the driver NEITHER replied in the chat within 120 seconds of the rider's message NOR placed an in-app voice call before terminating. The driver did both. He posted messages at 08:43:00, 08:45:20, 08:49:30 and 08:50:45, and the trip record carries in-app call CALL-00901-001, initiated by the DRIVER at 08:47:05 and unanswered after 22 seconds. On either limb the rider-exonerating clause does not apply and no refund flows from it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d) are satisfied on the platform's own records. Limb (a): the trip record contains a driver 'arrived' event for this trip at 08:43:00, auto-confirmed from a GPS measurement. Limb (d): there is no boarding event, the trip status is CANCELLED_BY_DRIVER, and it terminated at 08:51:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW — one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. The rider-displacing clauses POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 do not fire (argued below), so the fee stands as itemised.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The dwell limb is corroborated by a clean artifact independent of the GPS. The chat log, at weight 1.0, shows the driver present and waiting from his 08:43:00 message — 'I've arrived at the pickup point, I'm at the lobby area' — through his 08:50:45 message — 'Please let me know, otherwise I'll have to cancel the trip' — with intermediate messages at 08:45:20 and 08:49:30 identifying the vehicle (white Honda HR-V, SGP 4521 M). That is 480 seconds of continuous presence at the pickup, comfortably above the 300-second STANDARD minimum, closing only when the SYSTEM logs the cancellation at 08:51:00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.first_message_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose that the GPS trace on which the rider's arithmetic must rest is IMPAIRED: issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD, weight_multiplier 0.6. Five of its seven inter-fix intervals (180, 240, 180, 120, 120, 180, 180 seconds) exceed POL-NS-08(b)'s 120-second gap limb, the waiting window holds only four fixes against the six that limb requires, and no rider track was supplied. Under POL-GEN-02(1) that impairment must be stated in the same claim that cites it, and under POL-NS-08 a claim resting on this artifact is down-weighted: it cannot alone support a ruling against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "gaps",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's cleanest arithmetic route is POL-NS-02, but the clause cannot carry it here. POL-NS-02's own drafting note states that a trace too sparse to establish three consecutive in-radius readings is 'impaired under POL-NS-08(b) rather than proof of absence'. This trace is exactly that shape — four fixes inside the waiting window, with no accuracy data. The absence of a qualifying in-radius fix is an impairment of the record, not a demonstration that the driver never arrived, and the clause's stated consequence (limb (b) fails, full refund) does not attach to a trace the clause itself classifies as impaired. (The trace is impaired: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-02 admits only fixes whose reported horizontal accuracy is 25 m or better, and not one fix in this trace reports any accuracy field at all. The derived qualifying_fix_count of 0 therefore measures the trace's missing data, not the driver's conduct: on its own terms the clause's proximity test cannot be run, and the policy itself says such fixes 'count as evidence of neither presence nor absence'. The zero dwell figure cannot be turned into an affirmative finding against the fee. (The trace is impaired: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 sets aside an arrival marker only where the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin at the marker, or shows him travelling at 15 km/h or above. Neither is established here. The pre-pass records no clock skew — the 08:43:00 marker is the nearest fix timestamp to the second, so POL-NS-08(a) is not engaged — and the driver's own track records a minimum distance to the pickup pin of 0 m across its fixes, with a mean of 274 m and a maximum of 1,109 m, the profile of a vehicle that drove up to the pin and held there. The marker is not false on this record and the waiting clock runs from it. (That derived minimum is drawn from the impaired trace: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 refunds a rider only where the effective in-geofence dwell, computed under POL-NS-02, falls short of the minimum for the zone class. No such dwell is computable here, because no fix carries the accuracy POL-NS-02 requires, so the clause's premise cannot be established on this record. Its accumulation limb (i) is expressly unavailable as well: EV-ADVIS-00901-01, the traffic advisory, is MISSING, and limb (i) requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated. A MISSING artifact keeps its identifier, carries weight 0.0, and can carry no fact; it cannot be asserted against, and it exonerates no one. The shortfall arithmetic therefore proves nothing against the fee. (The GPS trace is impaired: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901", "EV-ADVIS-00901-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account — that they were at the lobby and the driver was not — has no location evidence behind it at all. The trace carries no rider track (rider_fix_count 0), and under POL-NS-04 limb (c) an absent rider track is expressly neutral: the rider-presence test cannot be run and must be recorded as unrun rather than inferred either way. The only record of the rider's whereabouts is the claim text itself. The driver's whereabouts, by contrast, are carried by the platform's own auto-arrival marker and by six timed chat entries over an eight-minute window. (The trace is impaired: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "If the fee is found chargeable, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's compensation at 80 percent of the itemised cancellation fee, and the anti-farming bar cannot trip. That bar withholds compensation only where driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 4 or more AND exceeds 0.08 of driver_profile.completed_trips_30d; the field is null on this record, which is not '4 or more'. POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter for the trailing-30-day figure this clause names, so the check does not engage and compensation is payable — the derived money block computes the driver compensation at SGD 4.00. I disclose that the fare ledger supporting the amount is impaired (PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.75).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901", "EV-DPROF-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Judge concludes the record cannot settle arrival and dwell, the disposition that protects the fee is escalation, not refund. The trip record's auto-arrival marker and the GPS trace's zero qualifying fixes contradict each other directly on arrival and on dwell, and no clause resolves that conflict because the trace is accuracy-blind — POL-NS-09(b). In the alternative, the sole evidence for the deciding dwell fact is the trace, impaired under POL-NS-08(b), which caps the ruling at PARTIAL_REFUND and sends the case to the human reviewer under POL-NS-09. On either path the disputed fee is held rather than refunded while review is pending. (The trace is impaired: LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose a further defect rather than leave it to my opponent: the fare ledger is IMPAIRED — issue code PARTIAL_RECORD, weight_multiplier 0.75 — and its SGD 5.00 cancellation line does not reconcile with the fee schedule, which yields SGD 4.00 as the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00). That mismatch engages POL-NS-08(d). It is a defect in the amount recorded, not in the chargeability of the fee: it cannot convert a legitimate no-show charge into the full reversal the rider seeks.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.difference",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    }
  ]
}

