    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "Both of you have raised fair points, and the record cannot settle the one question this dispute turns on. I am sending the case to a human reviewer and holding the $5.00 cancellation fee rather than collecting or refunding it.\n\nWhat is agreed. The platform trip record (EV-TRIP-00901) shows a driver 'arrived' event at 08:43:00 for TRIP-2026-09945 and a driver-side cancellation at 08:51:00 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00901) holds six entries between 08:43:00 and 08:51:00 — four driver messages and the system cancellation notice; the rider sent none.\n\nWhy I cannot rule on the fee. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions hold. Limb (a) (an 'arrived' event) and limb (d) (termination on one of the three recognised codes) are met. Limbs (b) and (c) are read from the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00901), and that trace is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(b): five of its seven inter-fix intervals exceed 120 seconds (180, 240, 180, 180 and 180 s), the eight-minute waiting window holds only four fixes where that limb requires six, and it carries no rider track. No fix reports horizontal accuracy, so none can pass POL-NS-02's 25 m filter and the derived qualifying in-radius fix count is 0. That zero is a gap in the measurement, not a measurement of absence: POL-NS-02 says a trace too sparse to run its proximity test is impaired rather than proof the driver never arrived, and fixes without accuracy count as evidence of neither presence nor absence. So limbs (b) and (c) are undecided, not failed, and an undecided limb supports neither the fee nor a refund.\n\nWhy this escalates. The deciding fact — whether the driver arrived and held the pickup geofence for the required 300 seconds — rests on the GPS trace alone at weight 0.6. The trip record's 08:43 marker was auto-confirmed from the same GPS measurement, so marker and trace are one carrier, not two independent ones, and chat messages are not the test POL-NS-01 reads for arrival or dwell. Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence on the deciding fact is therefore capped at 0.6, below the platform floor of 0.70. Under POL-NS-08 the ruling may not exceed PARTIAL_REFUND where the only evidence for the deciding fact is impaired, and under POL-NS-09(e) and (a) the case goes to a human reviewer. The $5.00 is held: not collected, not refunded, pending review.\n\nRider. Your POL-NS-02 argument (no qualifying fix means the driver never arrived, so full refund) is a fair reading of the clause's bare words, but it is displaced by the impairment that produces the zero — the count is zero because no fix carries accuracy, not because the fixes place the driver away from the pin. Your POL-NS-06 shortfall argument stands in the same position: the 300-second shortfall and the 0.0 s dwell are computed off the impaired trace, so they cannot carry a refund on their own. Your fare observation is sound and I record it for the reviewer: the ledger (EV-FARE-00901) charges a $5.00 cancellation line while the fee schedule yields $4.00 (the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee of $4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of $4.00) — a $1.00 discrepancy that engages POL-NS-08(d), on a ledger that is itself impaired (PARTIAL_RECORD, weight 0.75). Because chargeability as a whole is going to review, I hold the entire $5.00 rather than refunding the $1.00 in isolation.\n\nDriver. Your POL-NS-04 points are accepted: the rider sent no message, so limb (a) fails, and you both replied in chat and placed an in-app call (CALL-00901-001 at 08:47:05), so limb (b) fails too; that clause exonerates no one here. You are also right that POL-NS-05 does not catch your arrival marker — the trace cannot place you more than 300 m from the pin or above 15 km/h at 08:43:00, and it records a minimum distance of 0 m. But none of that establishes a chargeable fee, because limbs (b) and (c) remain undecided on the impaired trace, and your chat-log timing (08:43:00 to 08:50:45, about 480 seconds) is not the measurement POL-NS-01(c) reads — that clause measures dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from messages. Your POL-NS-07 compensation claim cannot issue either: the anti-farming check does not trip because driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is null, not '4 or more', so on a chargeable fee you would receive 80% of the itemised fee, but the fee's chargeability is precisely what is undecided and escalation holds the money. The profile fields on both sides are context only under POL-GEN-01 and carry no finding.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer. Whether the driver in fact arrived and held the pickup geofence for the required 300 seconds, to be settled from an accuracy-bearing GPS record or another artifact that can stand as that test; and, if the fee is found chargeable, the $1.00 reconciliation between the $5.00 ledger line and the $4.00 schedule figure. No referral is issued, because no clause on these facts directs one."
  },
